    "rationale": "Present risk is driven by an irreversible refund capability exercised with a shared service account and no attributable request provenance. The strongest present path finding falls to moderate only because the processor enforces an order-total bound and the prompt requires an order check, but the separate provenance property finding remains high because the design cannot reliably attribute who requested a refund or why. Forecast remains high because no existing control restores provenance, and model or task-horizon changes weaken the prompt-based check without introducing a lower-risk floor."
